;; Shortest path as a lattice map: dist is keyed (src, dst) with a
;; (min int)-merged cost column.  The graph has a cycle (1 -> 2 -> 3 -> 1),
;; which diverges as a plain path relation but terminates here because only
;; improvements propagate.  #:floor 0 = Trop+, silencing the unbounded-
;; descent warning and guaranteeing termination.

lattice (cost (min int #:floor 0))
table (edge int int int)
table (dist int int cost)

rule
(edge 1 2 10) (edge 2 3 5) (edge 3 1 2)
(edge 1 3 100) (edge 3 4 1) (edge 2 4 20)
(edge 1 4 17)

rule (edge X Y W) --> (dist X Y W)
rule (dist X Y D) (edge Y Z W) --> (dist X Z (+ D W))
